  "prefLabel": "Ins 2602.11 Conflict With Other Laws or Rules",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 2602.11 Conflict With Other Laws or Rules. It is not intended that this part conflict with or supersede any rules currently in force or subsequently adopted in this state governing specific aspects of the sale or replacement of life insurance including, but not limited to, laws or rules dealing with life insurance cost comparison indices, deceptive practices in the sale of life insurance, replacement of life insurance policies, illustration of life insurance policies, and annuity disclosure. Consequently, no disclosure pursuant to or required under those rules shall be deemed to be an advertisement within the meaning of this part.\n\nSource. #9333, eff 12-5-08; ss by #11173, eff 12-5-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins2600.html"
